# An object's prototype link still counts as unchanged when plain objects that shadow nothing are between the object and its class's prototype.
# The prototype of a subclass is such an object once it has lost its own properties.
# Out of the compiler's sight, the prototype of an Animal is set to the stripped Dog.prototype, so that Animal is a Dog.
# So the layouts of the superclasses of the tested class are not sibling layouts.
# Fault injection, testing=SkipSuperclassCheck: they count as sibling layouts.
# With --aot-harden=proof-checks (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime) each result derived from shapes is checked against a walk of the prototype chain that gives up at a trap and runs no code.
# If they disagree, the process crashes.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: 2 3
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(WRONG): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=SkipSuperclassCheck
# WRONG: 2 2
# WRONG-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=SkipSuperclassCheck,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HELD: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# HELD-NEXT: in the result of an operation
# HELD: crashed with SIGABRT
# -- source: main.ts
